WHAT THE MIT LICENCE ABOVE COVERS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT

Covered — take it, change it, ship it, sell it:
  index.html, map.config.js (the structure), bake_alpha.py, rematte.py,
  verify.mjs, the .claude/ skill, and the documentation.
  This is the engine, and it is the thing this repository exists to give away.

NOT covered:
  · The example map content. The map currently describes JAKE VAN CLIEF's life and
    career. That is his biography, not the author's to license. It ships so the engine
    has something real to draw. Replace it with your own — MAKE-YOUR-OWN.md is the
    whole guide to doing exactly that.
  · The illustrations in assets/ and demo/. These were made for this specific map and
    are shared to show the engine working, not as stock art. Generate or draw your own.

In plain terms: the machine is yours. The life on it isn't.
